        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0864" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg768"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Press Release Issued by the Department of State on
                        June 3, 1938</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1938-06-03">June 3, 1938</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">Excerpt from press conference record. Not to be quoted, but
                    may be used in third person as having been said by the Acting Secretary of
                    State, Mr. Sumner Welles.</p>
                <p>The American Government has observed with gratification the steps which the
                    Japanese Government has taken. There remain of course other questions which need
                    to be taken care of. There is the question of the return to the American owners
                    of the property of the University of Shanghai in the Yangtzepoo district of
                    Shanghai. There is the question of other American properties in the lower
                    Yangtze Valley. There is the question of removal of obstacles to the return of
                    American missionaries to their properties in places other than Nanking. There is
                    the question of the return of American businessmen <pb facs="0865" n="769"
                        xml:id="pg769"/> to their properties in Nanking and in other places in the
                    lower Yangtze Valley. This Government is confident that the Japanese Government
                    will promptly take appropriate action with regard to these matters.</p>
            </div>
